<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Install",
    subtitle: "Set up the host app, migrations, seeds, and optional Active Storage support for RecordingStudio Publishable.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "What the generator does",
        subtitle: "The install generator prepares the host app for publishable child recordings."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--surface-muted-content-color)]">
        <p>Run the generator from the host app to mount the engine, copy the migrations, and add the initializer.</p>
        <p>It also appends a seed snippet, and can create an environment-specific config file when you want one.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Typical install flow",
        subtitle: "Use the generated initializer and migrations as the base for the addon."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :bash,
        code: <<~CODE
          bin/rails generate recording_studio_publishable:install
          bin/rails db:migrate
          bin/rails db:seed
        CODE
      ) %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Optional Active Storage support",
        subtitle: "Install Active Storage before using the social_image attachment field."
      ) %>

      <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
        language: :bash,
        code: <<~CODE
          bin/rails active_storage:install
          bin/rails db:migrate
        CODE
      ) %>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
        title: "Review the seed snippet",
        subtitle: "Replace the example lookup or provide the parent recording id before seeding."
      ) %>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--surface-muted-content-color)]">
        <p>The generated seed block uses <%= link_to "ENV.fetch", "https://ruby-doc.org/core-3.3.0/ENV.html#method-c-fetch" %> for the parent recording id, so you can safely provide it in the shell or update the lookup for your app.</p>
        <p>If you use Tailwind CSS, keep the engine and FlatPack source paths in your Tailwind config before rebuilding assets.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
